												<div id="earlyAccessHeader" class="early_access_header">
		<div class="heading">
												<h2 class="inset">Early Access Game</h2>
					<p class="inset subtitle">Get instant access and start playing; get involved with this game as it develops.</p>
				
				<p><span>Note:</span> Games in Early Access are not complete and may or may not change further. If you are not excited to play this game in its current state, then you
									should wait to see if the game progresses further in development. <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/earlyaccessfaq/?snr=1_5_9_">Learn more</a></p>
					</div>
				<div id="earlyAccessBody" class="devnotes">
							<div class="devs_say">What the developers have to say:</div>
			
			<div id="devnotes_expander">
									<h3>Why Early Access?</h3>
					“With the game's core direction and structure now established, we chose to enter Early Access so that we can further refine the game based on the diverse experiences of actual players.<br />
<br />
During Early Access, we hope to see how well our intended gameplay and sense of fun translate into the actual player experience, and use what we learn to further improve the game as we work toward the full release.”
					<h3>Approximately how long will this game be in Early Access?</h3>
					“We expect Early Access to last approximately six months, with the full release currently targeted for the first half of 2027. The Early Access period may be adjusted depending on development progress and community feedback.”
					<h3>How is the full version planned to differ from the Early Access version?</h3>
					“The Early Access version includes approximately 50% of the content currently planned for the full release.<br />
<br />
For the full version, we plan to add new chapters that continue the story beyond Early Access, as well as additional endings. As the story progresses, players can expect new gameplay mechanics and story elements. We also plan to further refine and enhance the game's art and presentation.”
					<h3>What is the current state of the Early Access version?</h3>
					“The Early Access version currently includes six playable chapters, including the tutorial. All core gameplay systems and basic features, such as saving, loading, and settings, are implemented, and all currently available content can be played from beginning to end.”
					<h3>Will the game be priced differently during and after Early Access?</h3>
					“During Early Access, the game will be offered at a lower price than the full release version. With the full release, we plan to increase the price to reflect the expanded content and overall improvements to the game.”
					<h3>How are you planning on involving the Community in your development process?</h3>
					“We plan to gather player feedback and bug reports through the Steam Community and our official Discord server. We will review feedback on various aspects of the game, including balance, difficulty, and quality-of-life features, and use it to help guide updates and improvements.<br />
<br />
Throughout Early Access, we hope to work together with our players to further improve the game based on their experiences and feedback.”
							</div> <!-- /devnotes_expander -->
			<a class="morebutton" id="devnotes_more" href="#"  onclick="$J('#devnotes_expander').css({'max-height': 'none'}); $J(this).hide(); return false;">Read more</a>
		</div>
	</div>
										
					
